    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.files\n\n### Description\n\nHello,\r\n\r\nI want to change the current behavior of the navigation for my personal use. Would it be possible to expose the `H` table within the `mini.files` module?\r\n\r\nE.g. I don't want the navigation `go_in` to open the file and also add other custom explorer manipulations without forking the project.",
